    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7eaaf098-0baa-5d40-9ad4-12cd15f7e73b" activityNameId="761cc3fa-32cf-5385-bb6b-e19fd962bde9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, at 10.5 m2 evacuated tube collector, glass-glass tube, one-family house, for combined system</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, at 10.5 m2 evacuated tube collector, glass-glass tube, one-family house, for combined system
Use of a solar system with glass-glass pipes excluding the necessary auxiliary heating. The simulation is made for heat pipe solar collector systems in the city of Zurich. The annual irradiation amounts to 1249 kWh/m2. 33% solar fraction, 35° inclination, 22° southeast orientation.;
Synonyms: Sidney collector, China collector; 
UUID: dd89c76f-7e77-3cdb-b7d2-c18f314678f8
Delivery of heat with a solar system including maintenance and electricity use for operation. Excluding the necessary auxiliary heating. Rough assumption for a glass-glass tube collector system by considering a heat pipe system correcting the life time from 25 years to 20 years. 
Location: Solar collector system operated in CH.
Technology: Solar collector system for hot water installed on the roof of a house.
Time period: Time of simulation.
Production volume: Total solar heat delivered by evacuated tube collectors in 2001 was 2.3TJ.
Sampling: Own simulation. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_dd89c76f-7e77-3cdb-b7d2-c18f314678f8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
